COMPUTER SOFTWARE BASICS
1.	System software: manages hardware and provides platform for running application software
2.	Operating systems: manages resources (CPU Memory) asks files and provides a user interface Key functions include resource, task and file management
3.	Utility software: tools for system maintenance (e.g., antivirus backup disk defragmentation file compression)
4.	Application software: programs for end users to perform specific tasks (e.g., word processors spreadsheets)
