DATA ORGANISATION AND STORAGE
1)	Data Files: store data for applications no instructions
2)	Serial/Sequential Files: Records stored in the order in which they were created. Simple to read but slow to search (like a cassette tape)
3)	Random Access Files: records have a fixed length, allowing direct access to any record without reading all previous ones. Fast but can waste storage space
Storage terms:
	Track: A circular path on a disk
	Sector: A subdivision on a track
	Luser: A group of sectors managed by the operating system
